{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 100, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing edge with a 3x3 conv restores connectivity and gives big gains (runs 67, 72) versus small gains over other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty direct edge 0->3 with a conv gives large gains (run 86, 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a skip to a 3x3 conv on edge 4 gains more (run 85) than replacing an already-conv op."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on the input edge with a 3x3 conv gives consistent gains on all datasets (run 34)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pool-to-conv upgrades on edge 1 give large gains (run 32) compared with replacing a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a weak pooling edge into the output helps (runs 51, 87), whereas removing conv or skip edges hurts."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on edge 4 with skip loses capacity and hurts (runs 26, 44)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading the input conv to skip is damaging (run 75), unlike replacing weaker ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 1x1 conv on the output edge with pooling causes large losses (runs 61, 97)."}, {"edit_edg